================================================================
  musil: library reference (live)
================================================================

--- device ---
audio-devices    : 1 (a list of the playback devices' names)
audio-open       : opened; 44100 Hz, block 256 , 2 channels, device null
audio-start      : running 1
audio-time       : 1 (the clock advances, in seconds)
audio-report     : prints every field of audio-status (open, running, sr, block, channels, device, time, voices, load, peak)

--- voices ---
play             : voice 1 ; playing: 1
play-with        : amp, pan, rate, loop, at: 2
stereo           : 3 (a list of channels)
loop-buffer, set-amp/pan/rate: voice 4
stop, stop-all   : voices left 0
wait-for         : waited for voice 1 to end

--- time: sample-accurate scheduling on the clock ---
play-at t+0.2    : voice 5 waits for its time
wait-until       : now 1
sequence         : 2 voices scheduled at once

--- files ---
play-file        : voice 8 (any sample rate: the voice resamples)
play-file-with   : voice 9

--- synths ---
streamable       : (* + - / abs adsr allpass bandpass clip comb conv cos dc-block delay exp floor highpass highshelf iir lag list lowpass lowshelf max min noise notch osc pan peak-eq pow sin sqrt tanh)
offline call     : 2 channels of 8820 samples
synth            : id 10 , parameters (gate freq cutoff)
note-on          : sounding 1
set-param        : cutoff ramped to 200 over 0.2 s
note-off         : released 1
note             : gate on now, off in 0.1 s (scheduled)
free             : synths 0
play-synth       : id 11 (compile, set, gate on)
synth-render     : the graph offline; equals the call within 1
not streamable   : reference_live.mu:99: synth: not streamable: pvoc-stretch (see (streamable))
tables           : sine-table saw-table square-table triangle-table, for osc

--- loops ---
tempo, bpm, beat : 120 bpm; beat 1 ; beat-time of beat 2 minus beat 0: 1 s
live-loop        : loops (bassline) ; the function named bassline runs every 2 beats
redefine         : function bassline ... again; the next cycle uses the new one
stop-loop        : loops ()
ev, ev-beat      : (0 2) (an event is (list beat dur thunk); the thunk gets the time and duration)
fast, slow, shift: (0 1) (0 4) (1 3)
rev, every       : (3 1) (0 1)
cat, stack       : (0 2 4 6) 4
steps            : (0 1 1.5) (nil is a rest)
synth-ev, play-ev: events on a synth (parameters + gate) or a buffer

--- controls and osc ---
control, toggle  : ((cutoff 100 5000 1200 0) (on 0 1 0 1))
set-control      : cutoff now 300 (the bound synth followed, ramped)
controls         : opens the controls window (sliders and check boxes) and returns; (controls-open?) tells if it is
osc-send/listen  : after a message to /cutoff, the control is 2000
serve            : (serve 7770) opens the evaluation port editors send code to; (serving) tells which

--- closing ---
audio-stop       : running 0
audio-quit       : open 0

================================================================
  end of live reference
================================================================
